#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d451b05-a3cf-5777-a459-c28d94c790cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340470} {:answer/id #uuid "e42a7588-d111-5478-b34b-95670c6d36d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340471} {:answer/id #uuid "9d3a7318-2ac6-57d8-aabe-645d5a38808a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340472} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb4d354-ab4d-5892-9cfa-e868adccf1eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340473} {:answer/id #uuid "9baf7df9-92ad-526b-85f8-aa369c591006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d3a7318-2ac6-57d8-aabe-645d5a38808a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340472} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a3e6589-0302-58b9-9b99-420e1cb34413" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4108dba5-a98f-50ab-8fa7-798c7ddb7f0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-105160" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$ given that $3a-5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a-5x & =b \\\\ -5x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}-13 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5176f94c-b3d7-55f0-9831-90bc130fe9b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340477} {:answer/id #uuid "04b6a111-8cac-5c02-9414-65cd5b91df66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340478} {:answer/id #uuid "4b22f19e-e9b4-54cc-8cd4-9986bf169493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340479} {:answer/id #uuid "88b2e377-967b-5de7-a80d-5baf2cd84ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340480} {:answer/id #uuid "f13db315-f288-5d89-bada-ac6e93226221" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04b6a111-8cac-5c02-9414-65cd5b91df66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340478} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d7a11e8-42ec-55ae-a6a2-8e71f70e7335" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f4cc426-8edc-5853-97ca-58831fd58674" :question/math-academy-id "q-105167" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2}=-9 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5(3) & =3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ (4)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ which means\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+3=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2f20cc7-771d-5044-ba85-ba83e0b94627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340484} {:answer/id #uuid "7c30856c-03d5-56c4-bb1b-377ab9fe821a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340485} {:answer/id #uuid "7bcd222c-0104-570f-8f16-602a9cb65046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340486} {:answer/id #uuid "af33eac0-fead-5aa4-b942-7ed01bb02efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340487} {:answer/id #uuid "582eedc7-c97b-5fc7-8ce3-eb42318ed701" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f20cc7-771d-5044-ba85-ba83e0b94627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340484} :answer-field/id #uuid "f264819e-3819-5dc5-97dc-3265241aee8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340483}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "699da302-dc6b-5ab6-a923-64ab693ea43f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34601" :question/problem "Find the value of ${x}_{3}-{x}_{4}$ given that  $6a-2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a-2x & =b \\\\ -2x & =b-6a \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}(b-6a) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-16 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -48 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 29\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=24-29=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94cf71a5-f8ef-5532-a031-12ce96ac2b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340491} {:answer/id #uuid "ab1728ec-9dc5-5478-b27b-eeb2b310bece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340492} {:answer/id #uuid "16a743f7-e4e3-5d42-9e43-e42ea305e97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340493} {:answer/id #uuid "72d7c196-9c5f-5d5e-a08a-07caafcfb195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340494} {:answer/id #uuid "4205870b-a3f8-5699-9ead-23401f0c49e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab1728ec-9dc5-5478-b27b-eeb2b310bece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340492} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0384bab-b8d7-5abd-89f3-0cb9d80d27c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340490}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9890d0f-a574-5442-8aa8-be48658bceab" :question/math-academy-id "q-74006" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then   we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ 0=-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-12$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186340496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0fe467a-2dce-51a7-8f4b-e6ab0a9425f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340498} {:answer/id #uuid "7495ac1a-eec6-562b-b0c1-bfde9ebd34ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340499} {:answer/id #uuid "19eafb9c-823d-51b5-942f-a440bdfc1cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340500} {:answer/id #uuid "37b19c26-618f-536e-9d18-d253ddfc349b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340501} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea5e1b9-2c80-508a-8cf6-48716e54d21b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ea5e1b9-2c80-508a-8cf6-48716e54d21b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340502} :answer-field/id #uuid "948b8786-95d1-58a2-94ad-53d105929fbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340497}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4659fe52-f91a-51a6-a6b4-a2d78caaefe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-74035" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0.2 & 0.8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{2}+\\,0.2{x}_{3}=0.8 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+0.2(-1)=0.8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n   \n\nFinally,  substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-2$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means  \n\n$$\n-2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-2+1-1=-2.\n$$"}]}
